it\nfor future commit and branch work.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"md":{"insertions":58,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"81e3c85d67d020073a924d7f95e90df77769b48c","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge branch \u0027branch-A-CodingStandard\u0027","messageBody":"Project-specific Java and Git standards need to be available on the\nmain development branch.\n\nMerge the coding-standard skills, agent mandates, and Java\ndocumentation compliance changes into master.\n","tags":["A-CodingStandard"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"939131a7b1ff79c249f2ffe76b7142be5e33d088","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add Find support","messageBody":"Yachiyo cannot locate tasks by description without listing the entire task collection.\n\nAdd a read-only find command that performs case-insensitive keyword matching and retains original task numbers.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":105,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"c70f22fbd7397efac4490a3377d74d630749f7df","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add Find tests","messageBody":"Keyword search spans parsing, description filtering, numbering, and display behavior.\n\nAdd tests for case-insensitive matching, original task numbers, missing input, no results, and read-only execution.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":149,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"e2521758cdbdd5359181a8bf4de42202c29edcb3","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge branch \u0027branch-Level-9\u0027","messageBody":"Keyword task search needs to be available on the main development branch.\n\nMerge the find command, description filtering, Yachiyo output, and test coverage into master.\n","tags":["Level-9"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}}]},{"date":"2026-08-31T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"f9b6e447f5d3571357a9338070c0b5d5a9b6a5cc","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add CheckStyle","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"gradle":{"insertions":5,"deletions":0},"java":{"insertions":16,"deletions":32}}},{"hash":"5d1bd9b90d40b07593a9de3a2444275c2a3732e8","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge branch \u0027branch-A-CheckStyle\u0027","messageBody":"","tags":["A-CheckStyle"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"49413a9b506e2cf10f187de29ca0c5a8da8d2274","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Update variable naming","messageBody":"Use plural names for collection variables to clarify their contents.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":4,"deletions":4}}},{"hash":"599cf8015d2a7774531914126fdffe3c63521a12","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Update project documentation","messageBody":"Replace Duke template content with accurate Yachiyo setup instructions.\n\nDocument supported commands and usage examples in the user guide.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"md":{"insertions":161,"deletions":39}}}]},{"date":"2026-09-02T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"74c064742ceba9df122c30bcd9d61f91ecf1e48f","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add JavaFX dependencies and launchers","messageBody":"The project has no graphical entry point or JavaFX runtime support.\n\nAdd cross-platform JavaFX dependencies and application bootstrap classes\nso Gradle can launch the desktop interface.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"gradle":{"insertions":15,"deletions":1},"java":{"insertions":41,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"9456493a7d6726e41ef1fc079d0c3633ef7f7558","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add GUI for Duke","messageBody":"The JavaFX application does not present an interactive chat interface.\n\nAdd a basic chat window, message input, profile images, and dialog rows.\nAllow users to enter and view messages.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":88,"deletions":4}}},{"hash":"98456728b290ee6de9310ff4f5f7756ca5cc4a65","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add echoing","messageBody":"The chat interface does not react to submitted text.\n\nHandle button clicks and Enter key presses by adding the user\u0027s message\nto the dialog pane. Clear the input and keep the latest message visible.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":21,"deletions":5}}},{"hash":"1bb012baa89d7b0f487d5aaefb02f1cd1e463177","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add Yachiyo\u0027s response","messageBody":"The GUI only displays the user\u0027s submitted text.\n\nGenerate a temporary Yachiyo echo response and append it with a separate\navatar so both sides of the exchange are visible.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":20,"deletions":1}}},{"hash":"78782459166d812c6325584a1968631fad89cfb9","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Update DialogBox with custom behavior","messageBody":"Both sender types use identical alignment, making exchanges difficult to\ndistinguish.\n\nAdd named factories for user and Yachiyo dialogs. Flip the assistant\nnodes and alignment so responses appear on the left.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":39,"deletions":2}}},{"hash":"31d6ca5be99c8820491fa334e73fb7ef75b0a690","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Refactor to use FXML","messageBody":"The main window and dialog controls mix layout details with interaction\nlogic.\n\nMove view structure and styling into FXML resources, introduce a focused\nmain-window controller, and retain Main as the application bootstrap.\nPreserve Part 3 input, response, scrolling, and alignment behavior.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"fxml":{"insertions":76,"deletions":0},"java":{"insertions":112,"deletions":90}}},{"hash":"58f108caa913ec34f81d4ff3fda38b47e9d18b12","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Support responsive window resizing","messageBody":"The fixed layout leaves controls behind when the window changes size.\n\nAnchor the input, send button, and conversation pane to their container\nedges. Allow resizing while enforcing minimum dimensions that keep the\ninterface usable.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"fxml":{"insertions":8,"deletions":3},"java":{"insertions":2,"deletions":3}}},{"hash":"c84acef6dd25189618f79248c3a8697522ec91a7","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Connect GUI to task management","messageBody":"The JavaFX interface only echoes submitted text and does not use the\nexisting task manager.\n\nRoute GUI input through the parser, commands, task list, and storage.\nCapture command output for JavaFX, expose greeting and exit state, and\nadd integration tests for responses and persistence.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":204,"deletions":50}}},{"hash":"3e323e8002a9e3629134c1d46cc66ea8be564aa9","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add Yachiyo-themed chat styling","messageBody":"The functional chat uses the tutorial\u0027s plain visual presentation.\n\nApply a celestial color scheme, styled message bubbles, interaction\nstates, borders, padding, and shadows. Add supplied character and\nbackground assets with derived PNG profile images for the main window.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"fxml":{"insertions":5,"deletions":1},"java":{"insertions":1,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"0fff8f2684b9fa0b6ed55abcd1745ee3b3d8f5b4","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Polish main window interactions","messageBody":"The main window does not present the greeting and themed assets\nconsistently across sizes.\n\nDisplay the greeting and themed profiles when the GUI opens. Keep the\nanchored layout responsive, prevent startup clipping and pointer\noverlap, and ignore blank submissions.\n\nAfter bye, render the farewell, disable both input controls, and close\nthe window after a 1.75-second pause.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"fxml":{"insertions":27,"deletions":20},"java":{"insertions":35,"deletions":3}}},{"hash":"05f3e1a632cc91fc69a5d70f66f23be5a3cf3a21","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Fix delayed GUI exit","messageBody":"MainWindow is an FXML controller rather than the displayed root, so its\ninherited scene reference is null.\n\nResolve the stage through an injected control and keep the farewell\nvisible for two seconds before closing.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":2,"deletions":2}}},{"hash":"bd07ce21bc99751178b3eaf38cff94aeb16679fc","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge branch \u0027branch-Level-10\u0027","messageBody":"","tags":["Level-10"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"4f72826ef96d66b1127f2717b973578670960335","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Update project and user documentation","messageBody":"The documentation describes Yachiyo as command-line-only and directs\nIntelliJ users to the terminal entry point.\n\nDescribe the JavaFX workflow and correct launcher. Add a command summary,\ninput conventions, persistence details, and project structure.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"md":{"insertions":82,"deletions":30}}},{"hash":"2c6d936e02849c9b90ed734b86416ad884ef1d66","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add varargs TaskList constructor","messageBody":"Constructing a task list from a fixed set of tasks requires callers to\nwrap the tasks in a List.\n\nAccept fixed task arguments through a convenience overload while keeping\nthe list-based constructor for loaded collections. Verify that the new\nconstructor makes a defensive copy.\n","tags":["A-Varargs"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":14,"deletions":2}}}]},{"date":"2026-09-08T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"859cbc8ffa5c3a840923d2c3d731c6c2c4c39578","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add assertions for internal invariants","messageBody":"Several model, collection, lifecycle, and FXML assumptions are\nimplicit and can fail far from their source.\n\nDocument these invariants with Java assertions and enable assertions\nfor development and test runs. Keep external storage validation as a\nruntime error so correctness does not depend on assertions being\nenabled.\n\nAdd focused tests for the new invariant checks and malformed event\ndata.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"gradle":{"insertions":2,"deletions":0},"java":{"insertions":133,"deletions":3},"md":{"insertions":1,"deletions":1}}},{"hash":"670952cf7061d511c69ffc36a55bc0932739bcb6","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Extract event period parsing","messageBody":"Event parsing combines delimiter checks, date-time conversion,\nchronology validation, and object construction in one long method.\nThis obscures the successful path and makes each validation rule\nharder to inspect independently.\n\nExtract period parsing into a focused helper and represent the\nvalidated dates with a private EventPeriod record. Keep user-facing\nvalidation behavior unchanged while making parseEvent read at a\nsingle level of abstraction.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":23,"deletions":2}}},{"hash":"6ac0bc71b749f7a6372461d9c2aec26c24edfc6a","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Name command delimiter patterns","messageBody":"Parser split calls embed three similar lookaround expressions. Their\npurpose is difficult to infer at each use, and modifying the token\nboundary rule requires synchronized edits.\n\nCentralize the boundary rule in one helper and expose named patterns\nfor deadline and event delimiters. Keep the command syntax unchanged\nwhile making each parsing step state its intent.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":16,"deletions":3}}},{"hash":"456768f434a846e940f3d33738bc99c9671975a6","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Centralize task count formatting","messageBody":"Task-count messages repeat the same singular/plural expression in four\nUI methods. This obscures each message template and allows their\ngrammar rules to diverge during later edits.\n\nMove the shared rule into a focused formatting helper. Keep all\nuser-facing messages unchanged while giving future count formatting\none source of truth.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":11,"deletions":8}}},{"hash":"934247eb839d5fbd504add35aaf1cc78ec1d9e72","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Separate task record parsing stages","messageBody":"Storage.parseTask combines record validation, type-specific object\nconstruction, and completion-state restoration in one method. These\noperations sit at different abstraction levels and make the loading\nflow harder to scan.\n\nExtract task construction and status restoration into focused\nhelpers. Keep the serialized format and malformed-data behavior\nunchanged while making the orchestration method describe its steps\ndirectly.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":25,"deletions":4}}}]},{"date":"2026-09-09T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"d1e93443a939215666246f1f9d10b5aa528052f7","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Improve readability and reduce duplication","messageBody":"Several areas obscure intent with positional storage values,\nduplicate formatting and traversal logic, and a comment that restates\nthe following condition.\n\n- Name storage field positions, record sizes, task types, and status\n  values.\n- Share date-time formatting between deadlines and events.\n- Centralize numbered-task filtering and display.\n- Remove the redundant empty-input comment.\n\nKeep command behavior, stored data, result ordering, and user-visible\noutput unchanged.\n","tags":["A-FullCommitMessage"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":96,"deletions":54}}},{"hash":"ea717af84e5d2de6e7048d58422c7ad3a9264621","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Use stream to count incomplete tasks","messageBody":"TaskList calculates the remaining count with a mutable accumulator and\nan explicit loop.\n\nReplace that control flow with a filter-and-count pipeline to express\nthe operation as a collection query. Convert the long result exactly to\nretain the method\u0027s int return type.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":3,"deletions":7}}},{"hash":"c460919803089695b0e1199b5ac920b2328fe8c5","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #1 from robertlivando/branch-A-Assertions","messageBody":"Add assertions for internal invariants","tags":["A-Assertions"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"b2fa7d148b21f7aac3817b6a7bc5771cb1feedfb","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge branch \u0027master\u0027 into branch-A-CodeQuality","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"a82cef98808264a3ff8b6e068676aa92ca0eeb9e","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge branch \u0027master\u0027 into branch-A-Streams","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"e9da0406fd10bea93835b023c94086a6d902cebf","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #2 from robertlivando/branch-A-CodeQuality","messageBody":"Improve code readability and reduce duplication","tags":["A-CodeQuality"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"7a12aff586a1d3bf2d9aefbdb5cd3f7f22c0b428","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge branch \u0027master\u0027 into branch-A-Streams","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"d1ff20c30fb83e69a185e7d54aca559cf8b60cf1","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #3 from robertlivando/branch-A-Streams","messageBody":"Use stream to count incomplete tasks","tags":["A-Streams"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}}]}]},"authorFileTypeContributionMap":{"robertlivando":{"java":4176,"md":370,"fxml":92,"sh":0,"bat":0,"gradle":23,"txt":0}},"authorContributionVariance":{"robertlivando":605769.1},"authorDisplayNameMap":{"robertlivando":"CS2103T-F09-3 ROBE..ANDO"}}
